{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RLSA-2026:98060","published":"2026-11-13T12:06:37.188502Z","modified":"2026-11-13T12:45:07.737442155Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-19534","CVE-2026-84961","CVE-2026-85152"],"summary":"Important: nodejs26 security, bug fix, and enhancement update","details":"Node.js is a platform built on Chrome's JavaScript runtime for easily building fast, scalable network applications. Node.js uses an event-driven, non-blocking I/O model that makes it lightweight and efficient, perfect for data-intensive real-time applications that run across distributed devices.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* undici: undici: Authentication bypass via cross-origin cache poisoning due to missing origin isolation (CVE-2026-85152)\n\n* undici: undici: TLS certificate validation bypass in BalancedPool via dropped connect options (CVE-2026-84961)\n\n* undici: undici: Denial of Service via unrequested WebSocket subprotocol (CVE-2026-19534)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* Update Node.js 26 spec file for Rust package integration [rhel-10.3.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-256956)\n\n* nodejs26: Rebase to the latest Node.js 26 release [rhel-10.3.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-262243)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"nodejs26-docs","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/nodejs26-docs?distro=rocky-linux-10&epoch=1"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:26.8.2-1.el10_3"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"AppStream"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:98060.json"}},{"package":{"name":"nodejs26-npm","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/nodejs26-npm?distro=rocky-linux-10&epoch=1"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:11.19.1-1.26.8.2.1.el10_3"}],"database